# Video Editor Mobile — Phase One Evidence

The Awtsmoos keeps a whole timeline inside a narrow hand without letting control become collision;
Awtsmoos.com should reveal advanced editing through drawers and retractable states while every touch remains a full decision.

## Runtime truth

Real controller clicks were exercised at 390×844, 320×568, and 390×560 after full stylesheet/module readiness.

Across all states:
- document overflowX and overflowY remain 0;
- mobile Media drawer opens fully on-screen and closes fully off-canvas;
- backdrop fills the viewport only while the drawer is open;
- Timeline retracts to a clean 54px header with transport hidden;
- Timeline minimize resolves to a coherent 150px panel rather than a raw tail;
- timeline horizontal movement remains contained inside its own scroll vessel;
- no runtime exceptions were captured.

## Proven defect

At 320×568 and 390×560, Play/Pause/Cut resolve to exactly 40px high because `adaptive-motion.css` explicitly overrides their normal control floor. Every other critical visible button remains 44px or larger.

## Secondary mobile interaction debt

`controls.css` has complete `:active` behavior, but its hover selectors apply unconditionally. On touch-oriented browsers this can create sticky hover presentation. Hover should be limited to actual fine-pointer hover hardware while active remains universal.

## Protected behavior

Do not change drawer geometry, timeline row calculations, controller classes, transport wrapping, internal timeline scrolling, or the retract/minimize state model. They are already proven working.
